        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Apply consented grouped Claw updates",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- Extends experimental `claws update` from the read-only plan in #102959 to consented mutation across agent config, managed workspace files, packages, MCP declarations, cron jobs, and root provenance.\n- Requires both `--yes` and the exact `--plan-integrity` emitted by the latest dry run. Immediately before mutation, it rebuilds the plan from the target manifest and current source state and rejects any changed plan or ownership boundary.\n- Applies each owner through compare-and-swap checks and compensates completed owners in reverse order if a later owner fails.\n- Advances root package/version/integrity provenance only after every owner succeeds.\n- Reports `update_partial` when a real external installer or Gateway/config mutation may have retained state; preflight rejection, package reuse, and reference-only changes no longer claim retained artifacts.\n\nThis remains behind `OPENCLAW_EXPERIMENTAL_CLAWS=1` and is the mutation stage for the preceding read-only update plan.\n\nStack references:\n- RFC: openclaw/rfcs#27\n- Base/read-only planner: #102959\n- Control UI plugin lifecycle alignment: #103176\n\n## Lifecycle contract\n\n```bash\nopenclaw claws update <claw-or-agent> --from <source> --dry-run --json\nopenclaw claws update <claw-or-agent> --from <source> \\\n  --yes --plan-integrity <sha256-from-dry-run> --json\n```\n\nThe executor binds consent to the full plan, reloads current install/config/workspace/package/MCP/cron state, and fails closed when the target or current ownership has changed.\n\n- **Workspace:** rooted filesystem operations verify expected source digest, destination presence/content, and ownership before each write.\n- **Packages:** exact ClawHub versions use the shared installers. Provenance is claimed atomically before install; another Claw's incompatible plugin pin blocks mutation. Remove releases only this Claw's reference. Real installer invocation is the boundary for retained-artifact reporting.\n- **MCP:** validated config writes compare against the source config snapshot. Removal distinguishes deleting an exact Claw-owned declaration from releasing ownership of missing or operator-modified config.\n- **Cron:** Gateway-owned operations converge on stable Claw declaration keys and preserve explicit partial-state semantics for non-transactional scheduler writes.\n- **Provenance:** package, MCP, workspace, cron, and root records preserve complete timestamps and source/target integrity needed by status, doctor, retry, and rollback.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nAn isolated WSL2 Ubuntu 24.04 round trip previously exercised grouped preview, consented apply, and status for agent config, managed workspace files, and a remote OAuth MCP declaration. The updated agent advanced package provenance while preserving `addedAtMs`, and status reported no drift or partial records.\n\nThe final reviewed head also passes the real CLI lifecycle suite for inspect, read-only planning, consented add, workspace creation, status/remove, export, unsupported-component blocking, and missing-consent rejection.\n\nLive exact package replacement, Gateway-backed cron convergence, and retained-artifact diagnosis/recovery remain explicit maintainer proof requests before merge; their mutation, race, rollback, and partial-state contracts currently have focused injected/SQLite coverage.\n\n## Validation\n\n- 98 affected unit, runtime-config, and CLI tests pass across update planning/execution, package installation/provenance, workspace, MCP, cron, and CLI consent.\n- 8 real lifecycle E2E tests pass.\n- Real SQLite regression covers package reference replacement and rollback/upsert with complete timestamps.\n- Focused race regressions cover disappearing workspace targets, source MCP changes, concurrent package ownership, plugin preflight rejection, and reference-only rollback.\n- Touched-file `oxlint`, `oxfmt`, and `git diff --check` pass.\n- `codex review --base upstream/user/giodl/claws-pr11-update-plan`: no concrete actionable regressions.\n\n## Stack note\n\nThis is a draft stacked PR. Do not merge it before #102959 and the earlier Claws ownership/lifecycle slices settle.",
